What: /dev/fingerprint_dev retained standby ioctls
Date: October 2026
Contact: Doctor Logix <doctor.logix@gmail.com>
Description:
  UFF_FP_IOC_SET_STANDBY accepts a u32 boolean on the exclusive root-only
  control descriptor. The owner must first complete the signed sensor sleep
  command. One keeps the regulated supply/reset state, gates the IRQ and
  reduces the regulator load vote to 1 mA. Zero restores the active load
  vote/IRQ without reset. GET_STATE reports ABI version 1, powered, standby,
  and a physical reset generation. Reset in standby fails with EBUSY.
  Suspend is allowed only while powered off or in explicitly entered standby.
  Final close, including process death, always powers off and asserts reset.
  A load vote is not a measurement of actual sensor current.
